<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48243" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">thrŏnus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρόνος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an elevated
			seat</i>, <i>a throne</i> (syn. solium): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jovis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					35, 9, 36, § 63</span></i>
			; Poët. ap. <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Aug. 70</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dei,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Hamart. 10 praef.</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Auct. Pervig. Ven. 7: Thronos Caesaris,</span>”
				<i>one of the constellations</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					2, 70, 71, § 178</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An angelic order</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sive throni, sive dominationes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Col. 1, 16</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
